 using a foolproof  oral defense mechanism escapes  enslavement and convinces the parasites  to forego their reproductive urges to  live a longer more fulfilling life as a  result the parasites are able to quickly  build a sprawling society with media  matching skyscrapers and pearl harbors  and then  course Rick blows it all up - the twin  skyscrapers of course totally  it would have been cheap yeah real  low-hanging fruit we're better than that  also jerry has bees I think one of the  most interesting elements of this  episode lies in this small gag parasite  Rick Gloria - Brants against the  progressive agenda of living longer now  at first this seems like a quick jab at  people like alex jones did tonight at  least sell out and sell vitamins or  something but the basic concept is  mirrored everywhere in the episode that  is if something is natural does that  make it right  facehugger rick's argument for the  murder-suicide of hosts in parasite is  based on quote unquote science host of  course this is not actually science it's  the mention of science and a logical  fallacy we appeal to nature fallacy that  is the idea that if something is natural  it is inherently good desirable or even  inevitable this kind of fallacy pops up  everywhere in the debate about same-sex  marriage many people would argue that  homosexuality was unnatural and  therefore immoral then again getting  mauled by a tiger is perfectly natural  but that doesn't mean it's good this is  the appeal to nature fallacy in action  others would point to the fact correctly  that homosexuality is natural among many  of our closest animal relatives which  again is still a logical fallacy since  dictating where you can or can't stick  your genitals based on what does or  doesn't happen in nature is a logical  fallacy this fallacy also pops up around  the idea that might is right the idea  that people are justified to rule by  strength alone that claim usually gets  backed by citing Darwinism whatever  primates do or don't do in the wild or  our evolutionary history of humans being  dicks pretty much every time you hear  about monkeys primates or our cavemen  ancestors you should stop listening to  that person except that's a fallacy  fallacy dismissing a conclusion outright  because it's logic was flawed anyway  everyone shut up about monkeys already  parasite Rick's argument is exactly this  kind of appeal to nature he says we  should deposit our eggs because the host  can biologically sustain them he also  has a poster on his wall that displays a  kind of might is Right logic reading  that glory  our supreme and hosts are subservient  which echoes plenty of bad appeals to  nature found in places like social  Darwinism the progress of summer on the  other hand is about moving past biology  determining one's future let's just get  the hell out of here and be whatever the  [ __ ] we want that's evolution that's  progress but there's also a more subtle  critique going on here important to this  episode and life is that people when  appealing to nature often set up an  arbitrary divide between good nature and  bad nature oh yeah now you respect like  the biological institutions now you  people arguing that same-sex marriage is  bad because it's unnatural usually have  no problem watching YouTube for 8 hours  a day getting blood transfusions or  being temperature regulated by the  liquid remains of dinosaurs  similarly parasite rick has no problem  enjoying the unnatural spoils of  civilization or non-reproductive  arguably incestual face sucking while  railing against the repression of  biological processes inside this old man  yeah because I do what I want similarly  one could respect nature while despising  parts of it that seem a key or just  dangerous like snakes which have  historically been labeled in some  cultures as evil incarnate and of course  there's parasites which to my knowledge  don't really have too many positive  representations in the media it's pretty  much a default to think of them as  mindless their face hugging parasites I  don't think their society's gonna be  that hard to navigate and but here's  where the episode gets really  interesting because this looking down on  our face huggers is in a weird way a  mirror image of parasite rick normal  rick views parasites as lowly a lesser  form of life as rick and morty commit  mass murder they note how good it feels  to cause mayhem without guilt and feels  kind of good when there's no guilt just  like in Star Wars comparing it to  popping bubble wrap not destroying an  advanced civilization but this idea is  constantly undercut as the show likens  Rick and Morty's violence to American  tragedies so you did a 9/11 almost we  went with a Pearl Harbor we're pretty  classy why were either of those an  option or two even comments echoing  might is right justification for  destroying their world before becoming  horrified by his actions it's not all  that different than parasite Rick's  justification for enslaving host species  humans killing parasites is just some  old-fashioned natural pest control even  if by some unnatural means there's also  just a really interesting question here  that I love there's a basic hypothetical  is it fair to call a species evil for  just reproducing as their nature  dictates what would happen if we  encountered an intelligent alien that  could only survive by living  parasitically off another sentient alien  is there even a line in the sand we can  draw as a species that lives off eating  other species just some food for thought  and before we go I want to give one  final shout out to Paradox Interactive  and their strategy games stellaris  create and customize an empire to take  over the universe research other solar  systems and foster your Empire's economy  right now you can play for free by  clicking the link in the description  big shout out to our patrons for  supporting us and we'll see you next  time guys peace  [Music]  [